# .jacignore -- modules excluded from the repo-wide `jac check` gate.
#
# CI feeds every non-comment line here to `jac check --ignore` (see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml, "Run jac check (using .jacignore)"). CI adds
# `tests checker_*.jac *_err.jac` of its own; those are not listed here.
#
# Matching (compiler/frontend/helpers.jac:path_matches_exclude): an entry containing
# `/` is fnmatched against the whole path; a bare entry is fnmatched against
# EVERY path component, so a bare `types.jac` silences every file of that
# basename repo-wide. Every entry below is path-qualified for that reason --
# one line per excluded module, so a fix deletes exactly one line.
#
# Each entry is a module that does not currently pass `jac check`. Adding to
# this list is a debt, not a policy: the goal is an empty file.

# (stricter Unknown discipline). These files bind SQLAlchemy, ctypes, llvmlite
# .linkage etc.), not a new kind of exclusion.
# Bare name so any zig-pkg path component is skipped by the check step.
# Built-in shadcn handler + CLI (jac/jaclang/cli/shadcn) — dynamic `config: any` +
# CLI was renamed from plugin.jac/plugin.impl.jac to cli.jac/cli.impl.jac.
# External-library glue failing the full-repo jac check since ~2026-07-14
# Files failing the full-repo jac check as of the #7166 merge. The check
# Generated zig package fetches (jac ninja pins fetch into jac/zig-pkg/ at
# Impl annexes of modules already baselined above by bare name (lang_tools.jac,
# LLVM-IR builder submodules in this same category (ir.GlobalVariable/ir.Constant/
# Native wasm/LLVM emission + na_ir_gen ctypes-heavy submodules: bind
# Path, TextIOWrapper, JacProgram, Jac runtime, AST nodes, etc.
# Path-qualified so fixes/stubs can be shaved off file-by-file.
# Path/file-IO false positives (e.g. Path(__file__) in template discovery). The
# Re-enabled "has no attribute" diagnostic and __exit__ context manager check
# Stricter Unknown discipline -- these files have legitimate type gaps
# Vendored py2jac llvmlite translation (#6925): ctypes-heavy, intentionally not
# after ignore filtering runs -- so the annex paths must be listed too.
# and other untyped third-party APIs whose values the checker sees as
# build time; the tree-sitter-jac package ships its own examples/sample.jac).
# class as the passes/native/llvm and na_ir_gen entries above.
# create_target_machine) whose attrs the checker sees as Unknown, same class as
# cycle_collector/struct/debug/trace_fn.impl.jac (#7149) are na_ir_gen
# error in test_prim_equivalence.jac); #7166 fixed formatting, exposing
# explicitly, and an .impl.jac arg resolves to its (baselined known-bad) module
# expose false positives from incomplete Python type stubs. These files contain
# file-by-file.
# for `jac check`. fnmatch path-pattern -> matches every file under the package.
# lib.jac — jac-byllm and jac-scale pass, jaclang fails
# na_ir_gen/ / na_compile_pass.jac above. Skipped for `jac check`.
# object/<Unknown>; they can't be made type-clean without upstream stubs, same
# raw llvmlite/llvm-c handles (is_declaration, linkage, verify, emit_object,
# step had been masked for weeks by the format step failing first (syntax
# template_registry.jac, type_utils.jac). Scoped CI passes changed files
# that were previously silent (Unknown treated as Any). Added 2026-03-08.
# this accumulated debt. Path-qualified so fixes can be shaved off
# tools.jac — test fixture passes, others fail
# type-clean. jac format excludes it via the find in ci.yml; this skips it
# valid code that fails type checking due to missing stub coverage for str,
